
# Select: ONE component for the author, the platform's own picker underneath (native-dom-0026). The build fills
# `{platform}` from its env chain: macOS, iOS and Android reach ./native/toolkit/select.tree (NSPopUpButton, a
# UIButton showing a selection menu, a Spinner) through their `toolkit` rung, and every other target, the web among
# them, falls to the generic ./native/select.tree, the browser's own `<select>`. Both take `host`, `class`,
# `control` (the chosen option, a text signal) and `options` (the list to choose from). For a picker drawn by the
# theme rather than the platform, use `listbox`. See note/term/app/11-uniform-interface.md.
#
# This replaced a web-only wrapper whose options were `slot` children and whose change was a raw handler, a shape only
# a browser could honor, which nothing used.

bear @term/face/code/component/native/{platform}/select
